# Layout Reference

Use this reference whenever the final resume PDF is produced. It defines the default compact Chinese technical resume layout — a validated two-page template — and how to handle user-provided samples.

## Source Policy

If the user provides sample PDFs and TEX files:

1. Render the PDFs and inspect every page visually.
2. Read the TEX source for layout parameters and reusable commands.
3. Extract only layout rules, not private resume content.
4. Preserve the user's visual style unless they ask for a redesign.
5. Keep the resulting Skill documentation generic and publishable.

If no sample is provided, use the default template below instead of inventing a new layout.

## Default Template (Validated)

This layout produced a validated two-page Chinese technical resume: dense but scannable pages, no overflow, no orphaned headings. Use it as the default; deviate only for a user-requested redesign or a user-provided sample.

Visual characteristics:

- A4, single column, `11pt` base, sans-serif CJK/Latin font pairing, no page numbers.
- Header: centered — large bold name, then one line of `role · phone · email`, then a one-line positioning summary.
- Section titles: centered, bold, flanked by light gray rules spanning the text width.
- Project/entry heading: one line — bold name + small role on the left, gray date right-aligned.
- Inside project blocks: inline bold labels (not standalone heading lines) followed by text on the same line.
- Dates and auxiliary text in gray; key metrics bolded inline within bullets.
- `needspace` keeps each project block from splitting badly across pages.

Skeleton (placeholders only; requires an XeLaTeX-compatible engine such as `tectonic`):

```tex
\documentclass[11pt,a4paper]{ctexart}
\usepackage[margin=1.34cm,top=1.18cm,bottom=1.02cm]{geometry}
\usepackage{enumitem}
\usepackage{hyperref}
\usepackage{needspace}
\usepackage{fontspec}
\usepackage{xcolor}
\pagenumbering{gobble}
\hypersetup{hidelinks}

\definecolor{timegray}{HTML}{6B7280}
\definecolor{linegray}{HTML}{B7BCC4}

\renewcommand{\familydefault}{\sfdefault}
\setmainfont{Helvetica Neue}
\setsansfont{Helvetica Neue}
\setCJKmainfont{PingFang SC}[BoldFont=PingFang SC Semibold]
\setCJKsansfont{PingFang SC}[BoldFont=PingFang SC Semibold]

\setlength{\parindent}{0pt}
\setlength{\parskip}{0pt}
\linespread{1.24}
\setlist[itemize]{leftmargin=1.65em,itemsep=4pt,topsep=3pt,parsep=0pt}
\setlist[itemize,2]{leftmargin=1.5em,itemsep=2pt,topsep=2pt,parsep=0pt,label=\textcolor{timegray}{\scriptsize$\circ$}}

% Section heading: centered bold title flanked by gray rules.
\newcommand{\csection}[1]{\par\vspace{12pt}\noindent\makebox[\linewidth]{\color{linegray}\hrulefill\hspace{1.2em}{\color{black}\normalsize\bfseries #1}\hspace{1.2em}\hrulefill}\par\vspace{6pt}}

% Entry heading: bold name + small role left, gray date right; kept with its body.
\newcommand{\proj}[3]{\needspace{10\baselineskip}\par\vspace{9pt}{\bfseries \normalsize #1}\quad{\small #2}\hfill{\small\color{timegray}#3}\par\vspace{3pt}}

% Inline bold label with full-width colon, staying on the same line as its text.
\newcommand{\plabel}[1]{\par\vspace{1pt}\textbf{#1：}}

\begin{document}

\begin{center}
{\LARGE\bfseries <name>}\\[4pt]
{\normalsize <target role> \quad·\quad <phone> \quad·\quad <email>}\\[3pt]
{\small <one-line positioning summary>}
\end{center}

\csection{个人技能}
\begin{itemize}
  \item <skill group: mastery level + concrete usage>
\end{itemize}

\csection{工作经历}
{\bfseries <company>}\quad{\small <title>}\hfill{\small\color{timegray}<dates>}
\begin{itemize}
  \item <responsibility and platform status with \textbf{bold metrics}>
\end{itemize}

\csection{项目经历}
\proj{<project name>}{<dimension｜ownership level>}{<date range>}

\plabel{项目描述}
<one short paragraph: what the project is and its position in the overall narrative>

\plabel{项目架构}
<one stack line: language · framework · storage · key dependencies>

\plabel{责任描述}
\begin{itemize}
  \item <problem → designed/built → mechanism, with \textbf{verified metrics} bolded inline>
\end{itemize}

\csection{教育背景}
{\bfseries <school>}\quad{\small <college｜major｜degree>}\hfill{\small\color{timegray}<dates>}

\end{document}
```

Font note: `Helvetica Neue` and `PingFang SC` are macOS system fonts. On other systems, substitute available equivalents (for example Latin Modern Sans or TeX Gyre Heros for Latin, Noto Sans CJK SC or Source Han Sans for CJK, with a dedicated bold face) and keep every other parameter unchanged.

Adjust any value only after rendering and visual inspection.

## Page And Typography

- A4 paper, single column, base size `11pt`; do not shrink to `\small` before cutting weak copy.
- Margins: `1.34cm` left/right, `1.18cm` top, `1.02cm` bottom.
- Zero paragraph indentation, zero paragraph skip, line spread `1.24` so dense Chinese and mixed English text stay readable.
- Sans-serif pairing for both scripts; give CJK a dedicated semibold bold face so bold labels stay crisp.
- Two grays only: `#6B7280` for dates and auxiliary text, `#B7BCC4` for decorative rules. No other colors.
- Hide page numbers and hyperlink styles.

## Section Hierarchy

1. Header (centered): `\LARGE` bold name → `\normalsize` role/contact line → `\small` positioning summary.
2. Major sections via `\csection{...}`: centered bold text flanked by gray rules — visual separation comes from the rules and centering, not from large fonts.
3. Entry headings via `\proj{...}{...}{...}` or the company-line pattern: bold name + `\small` role on the left, `\small` gray date right-aligned on the same line.
4. Inside project blocks, `\plabel{...}` inline bold labels with a full-width colon: `项目描述`, `项目架构`, `责任描述`. Keep label names identical across all projects.
5. Bullets: first-level itemized lists; second-level rarely needed, styled as small gray circles.

Avoid cards, icons, boxes, or background fills; this layout's only decoration is the section rule pair.

## Project Block Pattern

For each major project, in order:

1. One-line `\proj` heading: project name, role/ownership dimension, date range.
2. `项目描述`: 1-3 sentences, including how this project relates to the others.
3. `项目架构`: a single stack line.
4. `责任描述`: bullets of the form problem → design/build → mechanism, with verified numbers bolded inline.

In this layout there is no separate outcomes label: quantified results live inside the responsibility bullets as bold inline metrics. Only add a separate outcomes label if the user's existing resume uses one.

## Page Break Strategy

- Target two pages for a senior technical resume; one page only when content genuinely fits.
- `\needspace{10\baselineskip}` in `\proj` prevents a heading from starting at the bottom of a page.
- Prefer keeping a project block intact over filling every blank space.
- Never split a `\proj` heading from its first `\plabel` paragraph.
- Education goes last and must not crowd project sections.

## Density Rules

- List spacing: first level `itemsep=4pt`, `topsep=3pt`; second level `2pt`.
- Labels stay on the same line as the text they introduce (`\plabel`), which saves one line per label compared to standalone label headings.
- Merge weak bullets before reducing font size; remove repeated stack wording before tightening margins.
- Keep line spread at `1.24`; compress content, not line height.
- Leave bottom whitespace if forcing more content would hurt readability.

## Visual QA

Render the PDF to images and check:

- header centering and contact readability
- section rules render in light gray, symmetric around each title, not clipped
- consistent left edge and bullet indentation
- clear distinction between sections, entry headings, labels, and bullets
- dates render in gray `#6B7280`; bold CJK (semibold face) is visibly heavier than regular
- no clipped CJK glyphs or awkward mixed Chinese/English spacing
- no section heading or `\proj` heading stranded at the bottom of a page
- no project header separated from its first label paragraph
- page two starts with meaningful content

Successful compilation is not enough. The layout reference is satisfied only after visual inspection.
